## Applying grid

The default grid is already built into the Figma layout component.

1. Select your grid type from the component properties panel.
2. Choose your breakpoint from the responsive menu in the appearance panel.

<img
	src={applyingGrid}
	srcDark={applyingGridDark}
	alt="Screenshot of the Figma layout component with the properties panel showing grid type and responsive selectors."
/>

You can also use this grid outside of the layout component. Select it from the assets panel in the
ADS Foundations library, or
[create your own](https://help.figma.com/hc/en-us/articles/360040450513-Create-layout-guides) using
your app's values.

**Tip:** Use **Shift + G** (Mac) or **Control + G** (Windows) to show or hide the grid in Figma.

